WEBVTT

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:05.230
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.530
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:24.790
Sheesh... I get it already, Mom...

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:28.500
You say that,
but are you really eating properly?

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.000
I am.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.760
I know you’re busy with work,
but you should come and visit sometime.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:35.890
Sure, sometime.

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:39.430
Do you have a special someone?
If you do, you should introduce us someda—

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:41.020
Oh, gotta go!

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.430
Sorry, I’ll call you when I can!

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:43.390
Kikuna?!

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:44.810
Sorry, Mom.

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:47.360
See you later.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.790
Today, there is bad weather
in Kuchiba City.

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:33.710
It is also rather cold.

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:39.680
You’re so energetic, Eevee!
But thanks to that, you’re keeping me warm.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:43.010
Actually, I wonder if there are Pokémon
that don’t like the cold...

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:46.970
I’m back, Dad.

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:48.560
Welcome back, Koharu.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:49.890
You’re leaving now?

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:54.980
Yeah. Oh, I’m always so excited
to see the newly-researched findings.

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:56.980
Director Sakuragi,
will you be all right?

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:58.780
The bus’ll be here soon.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:02:59.860
Oh, right!

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:02.200
Okay, I’ll be off.
I’ll leave the rest in your hands.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:02.700
Right.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.530
See you later!

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:09.160
Kikuna, are Go and Satoshi here?

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.790
Yes, they’re in the park right now—

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.380
C’mon, Go!

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:14.090
I told you to wait, Satoshi!

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:15.130
Oh, Koharu.

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:15.920
What is it?

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:18.550
Today’s forecast says
it’s going to snow!

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:22.550
And snow improves the odds
of seeing Ice-type Pokémon!

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:23.800
My chance to catch them!

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:25.680
Go!

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:27.310
I’m coming!

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:28.060
See ya.

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:30.180
When are you coming back?

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.190
Not until I catch something!

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:33.650
Whaaa...?

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:36.110
Did you have business with them?

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:38.320
I wouldn’t call it business,

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:40.190
but this morning...

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:46.450
Wait up, Wanpachi!

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:50.000
What’s going on this early...?

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:50.710
Sis!

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:54.250
Wanpachi?

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:56.750
Come on, Wanpachi...

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.000
What’s wrong, Sota?

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:01.590
I’m sleeping over
at Nami’s tonight.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:03.550
Oh, you are?

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:07.390
Everyone’s bringing
one of their family’s Pokémon,

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:10.770
so I wanna take
Wanpachi with me, but...

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:18.360
Wanpachi,
can you go with Sota?

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.320
Please?

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:27.120
Thanks!

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.580
Yes, I understand.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.250
I’ll try and do it.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.830
Yes. Okay then,
I’ll be going.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:36.670
Oh, Koharu.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:37.840
Did something happen?

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:42.670
Yeah... An illustrator I know
sprained their wrist...

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:44.630
What? Are they okay?

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:46.720
Apparently it’s nothing severe,

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:49.180
but they have magazine illustrations
due in two days,

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:51.430
so they asked
if I could draw them instead.

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:53.810
Um... You think you can make it?

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:57.900
They need three or so pieces,
so I should be okay if I start now.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:02.900
So I’m really sorry, but you’ll have to get
takeout or something for dinner, okay?

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.610
Got it. I’ll figure something out,

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.280
so you do your best, Mom!

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:08.830
Thank you!

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:13.250
So I thought I might have dinner
with Go and Satoshi.

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:14.290
Is that so?

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:17.790
With how they were,
they might not be back for a while.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:32.350
Gänger, you shouldn’t scare people.

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:37.100
Oh, that really scared me...

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:40.690
Maybe it’s in a bad mood
since Satoshi left it behind?

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:44.570
So what’re you going to do, Koharu?
Wait for Go and Satoshi?

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:48.200
Oh, given the occasion...
Could I watch you work?

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:50.490
Sure, go ahead!

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.080
Right. Yes.

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:56.080
If you could send us that data
straight away...

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:57.160
Yes...

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:58.210
Kikuna!

00:05:58.210 --> 00:05:59.580
Where was that thing?

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:02.420
In the folder
with yesterday’s date.

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:05.590
Ah, I see it!
Thank you so much.

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:10.010
Okay. Excuse me for a minute.

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:15.180
Seems something’s wrong
with the park’s air circulation system.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:17.020
Shall we take a look?

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:17.730
Sure.

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:22.190
It has been a cold day today.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:25.070
Maybe that got it busted up...

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:31.120
It was hiding in there?

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:37.710
This is it.
Messon probably hit this when it hid.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:43.420
Yep, all okay.

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:53.800
Kikuna’s really cool, isn’t she?

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:56.680
Yes! Thank you very much.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:58.680
I’ll be in contact. Goodbye!

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:02.060
That’s today’s work done.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:04.320
Go and Satoshi still aren’t back?

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:05.360
Doesn’t look like it.

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:09.360
Oh, well. Let’s just get
something to eat by ourselves, Eevee.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.370
Why not come home with me?

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:14.370
Huh?

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:16.410
I’d be all alone at home too.

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:18.540
Wanna have a girls’ night?

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:21.830
You don’t have school tomorrow, right?
You can stay over with me.

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:24.840
Oh, but, I...

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:30.930
Leave the braiding to me.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:33.640
I’ll teach you some
easy-to-do hairstyles, too.

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:34.550
Really?!

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:35.050
Yeah!

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:37.520
Th-Then I’d love to!

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:41.140
Okay. I’ll call your mother
and let her know.

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:42.690
I’ll leave the rest to you, Renji!

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:43.900
Oh, sure!

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:47.610
Eevee, we’re having a sleepover
at Kikuna’s place!

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:51.700
What would you like for dinner?

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:53.860
I’ll eat anything!

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.540
Let me know
if you see anything you’d like.

00:07:57.540 --> 00:07:58.580
Sure!

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:11.220
We sure bought a lot!

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:12.680
Yeah!

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:18.810
We’re here. This is my home.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:27.570
Stop that, Eevee!

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:30.570
I’m sorry. It’s a little messy...

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:32.700
...but I’ll tidy it up now!

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:38.990
Go on, make yourself at home.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.750
Uhh... Sure...

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:44.670
So this is Kikuna’s place...

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:50.340
You really like Koduck,
don’t you?

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:52.630
Yes.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:54.930
Something about looking at them
relaxes me.

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:58.140
So I tend to buy
Koduck merchandise, too.

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:01.100
You could just become
a Koduck’s trainer...

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:03.350
Just looking at them
is enough for me.

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:05.480
And...

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:11.570
Come on,
let’s eat while it’s still hot!

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:13.490
Oh, let me help!

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:20.370
There’s no Ice-type Pokémon
out here...

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:25.330
Temperature, humidity, pressure...
These are the best conditions, just as predicted...

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:27.370
So why?

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:30.420
Let’s go back.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:33.800
No! I’m not leaving
until I catch something!

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:36.130
Let’s just go back.

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:39.180
I’m starving...

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:41.310
I can’t wait till we get back...

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:42.720
Let’s just get something.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:43.600
Now you’re talking!

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:45.430
What do we get?

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:47.230
It’s cold,
so maybe ramen?

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:48.480
Sounds great to me!

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:09.580
Don’t do that, Eevee!

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.670
Sheesh...

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:19.050
It really did start snowing.

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:21.220
Do you think
Satoshi and Go are okay?

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:23.560
I-I’m sure they are.

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:24.850
Is something wrong?

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:26.560
I-It’s nothing!

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:28.560
Okay, let’s eat!

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:33.900
That man...
Is he Kikuna’s boyfriend?

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:36.940
Is that why she collects
Koduck merch?

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:42.530
I need to know!

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:45.120
Pocket Monsters!

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:57.670
Wow, it smells great!

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:00.840
Let’s eat!

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:05.850
Delicious!

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:08.350
Really? I should try one, too.

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:14.860
Tattsu-tei’s dim sum
has no equal!

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:19.360
Would you like to try one?

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:25.200
Looks like Eevee
likes them, too.

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:29.370
You’re already such good friends.

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:31.580
No, we have a long way to go.

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:35.750
I’d like to be closer,
but I’m not sure how to go about it...

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:39.720
Then why don’t you try asking
Satoshi and Go for tips?

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:43.180
No, I can’t...
They wouldn’t be any help.

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:46.180
What?! You don’t even know <i>that?</i>

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:51.600
You gotta be all “whumph” and “mmmph”
and “ahh...” with your Pokémon!

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:55.190
Oh, these look great, too!

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:57.940
One soy sauce ramen!

00:11:57.940 --> 00:11:59.360
Coming right up!

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:04.070
This is the best!

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:04.700
Yeah.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:08.540
I like to think the restaurants here
serve the tastiest food you’ll find.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:11.620
They really do.

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:13.670
A Koduck?

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:15.630
You’re right.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:17.500
That’s your Koduck?

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:18.710
Yeah, it’s mine.

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:21.630
It’s weird to see one
wearing a scarf!

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:23.180
It doesn’t like the cold.

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:25.550
That’s its favorite scarf.
It never lets go of it.

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:26.220
I see.

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:31.390
Koduck! Duck Pokémon!
Water type!

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:33.350
It is troubled by constant headaches!

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:37.560
The more pain it’s in,
the more powerful its psychokinesis becomes!

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:40.530
I-It couldn’t be...!

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:44.070
Koduck!

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:50.120
Koduck... It’s okay, it’s okay.

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:00.250
Sorry about that.

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:02.760
Let me get you something
to make up for the scare.

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:04.170
Oh, but...

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:06.550
I wanted to have the miso, too...

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:07.760
Okay, then I’ll get you that.

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:09.430
What?! Are you sure?!

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:11.890
I’ll have some more food, too.

00:13:11.890 --> 00:13:12.890
What about you two?

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:14.060
Oh, sure!

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:17.560
I’m stuffed!

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:20.440
Then I guess you don’t have
any room left?

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:21.690
You bet I do!

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:24.070
There’s always room for sweets,
isn’t there?

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:25.700
They all look tasty...

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:28.950
Then why don’t we have
half of each?

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:29.740
Sure!

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:34.910
Delicious!

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:39.960
They smell so nice...

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:40.920
Right?

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:42.460
They’re called essential oils.

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:48.090
Fabric soaked in oil can make a room fragrant,
or add scents to clothes in your closet.

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:50.010
What’s your favorite, Koharu?

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:52.140
Hmm... Maybe this one?

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:56.600
That one uses oil
extracted from Roselia flowers!

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:58.810
Or if you like sweet scents,

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:01.610
you can even get
Amakaji- or Cuwawa-scented oils.

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:05.320
Pokémon research has its uses
even with stuff like this.

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:06.740
It really does!

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:13.620
Oh, Eevee...

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:21.000
Kikuna, this...

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:23.300
It fits perfectly!
That’s great!

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:26.970
I bought it because it was cute,
but it was too small for me!

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:29.010
I... I see...

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:33.470
I’m turning off the lights.

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:35.020
Okay.

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:44.480
That was fun.

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:48.360
It’s nice to have girls’ nights
every now and then.

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:51.910
I’ve learned a bit
about your private life,

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:54.700
and I was really shocked
to find out you were so bad at cleaning!

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:57.500
Please, pretend you
never saw that!

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:02.880
Kikuna... You work hard,
you’re beautiful,

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.880
you’re a huge inspiration for me...

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:07.880
I’d like to be someone like you.

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:12.300
It’s not like it’s always been
smooth sailing for me.

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:18.020
One time I messed up so badly
that I almost gave up on being a researcher.

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:20.100
You did?

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:23.020
It was this enormous catastrophe.

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:25.820
Back when I was a student,

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:29.820
I was supposed to do
a research presentation at a conference.

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:33.910
I was hoping it would be well-received
so I could become a researcher.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.660
But the day of the conference...

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:38.080
I lost the data I was going to present.

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:40.830
What?! S-So what happened?

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:44.040
Of course,
I couldn’t do the presentation.

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:45.920
I was really depressed.

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:50.670
I felt terrible,
thinking I couldn’t be a researcher.

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:51.720
And then...

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:10.610
Sorry, my Koduck...

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:13.610
...must’ve thought
you looked cold.

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:22.660
C’mon, Koduck.
Let’s keep going.

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:30.340
Maybe we should make it
a bit bigger?

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:33.180
Easy does it...

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:40.060
Come on, moving around
will warm you up.

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:48.570
Thank you.

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:50.820
Can I help, too?

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:53.820
Yeah, that’d be great!
Right, Koduck?

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.130
Now you’ve done it!

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:14.800
Here goes!

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:27.350
I was able to forget how cold and depressed I was
just getting to play around with them.

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:31.900
And that motivated me to keep trying
to become a researcher.

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:33.740
All that happened to you...

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:37.950
Whenever I’m feeling down,
that photo cheers me up.

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:41.700
Koduck merch helps bring back
memories of that day,

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:43.750
so I end up buying whatever I find.

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:46.250
What about that man?

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:47.870
I haven’t seen him since.

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:51.750
I wonder how he’s doing.

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:55.470
Kikuna...

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:00.100
See you then, Koharu.

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:02.220
Thank you for having me.

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:05.730
Oh, they’re back.

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:06.690
Hey, Koharu.

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:07.690
Morning!

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:12.150
So, did you catch any Ice Pokémon?

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:13.280
No luck.

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:15.490
It was really cold out there...

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:17.650
So we had a hot meal
and came back...

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:19.620
I see.

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:24.120
The guy who was sitting next to us
bought us two bowls of ramen!

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:27.710
He was so kind.
He had a weird Koduck with him.

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:28.710
Huh?

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:31.840
It was wearing a scarf.
He said it didn’t like the cold.

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:35.380
Was the scarf Koduck-patterned?!

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:37.380
Yeah, it was... Why?

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:38.800
Where is he now?

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:39.470
No idea.

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:40.180
Koharu?

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:41.180
I want to meet him!

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:43.680
It’s not like
<i>we</i> know where he is...

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:03.910
Hey, forget about it.
This is impossible.

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:07.200
We didn’t even get his name...

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:09.920
And he didn’t say
where he was going.

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:16.130
I’m sure Kikuna
wants to see him...

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:26.390
Koduck?

00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:30.730
Oh, the one from yesterday!

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:33.230
That means...

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:34.610
Sorry!

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:37.110
H-Huh? You guys...

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:39.110
The ramen guy!

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:40.950
It’s a miracle.

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:45.700
Um...

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:47.450
There’s someone
I’d like you to meet!

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:48.790
Huh?

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:55.460
Kikuna!

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:56.670
Oh! Koharu!

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:59.380
Kikuna, I found him!

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:01.510
Hey, easy...

00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:08.720
Um...

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:12.350
I...

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:15.810
...never thought
I’d see you again...

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:40.340
I’ve longed to see you, Koduck!

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:40.840
Huh?

00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:44.930
The scarf you gave me back then
was so warm.

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:48.640
Playing together in the snow
made me so happy.

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:53.560
Ever since then,
the thought of you has kept me going!

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:54.690
Thank you!

00:20:59.190 --> 00:20:59.900
Koharu?

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:00.690
What is it?

00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:04.950
Oh, you’re that snowman girl!

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:09.370
So it was <i>Koduck</i>
you wanted to meet...?

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:21.130
Did something nice happen?

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:23.720
Yes, an emotional reunion!

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:25.880
I got lots of photos, too!

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:28.510
Thank you, Koharu!

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:32.770
People and Pokémon...

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:36.350
Everyone has their own unique way
of meeting and bonding with others.

00:21:36.350 --> 00:21:40.020
But once forged,
those bonds are sure to become...

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:42.780
...an everlasting
source of comfort.

